That's mostly a matter of becoming better at getting faster and tougher.
Pets are most of the key; tough pets, as many pets as you can tame (all
aside, even a kitten with 1 hitpoint is a perfectly good barrier),
pet-test and try armour. And don't blunder around the Mines in the dark
asking for nasty surprises to run up to you.

>Another situation I find it useful is when facing off with something
>like Demogorgon.

Well, there aren't many people like Demogorgon, and indeed key one to
dealing with Demogorgon is absolute minimisation of the risk of having to
deal with him. Jubilex and Yeenoghu can both be safely stowed away by
same-race sacrifices if you are Chaotic; Jubilex can be dispatched in two
rounds; Orcus should be dispatched as quickly as possible. If you come up
into Orcus town and he isn't next to you there and then, it's back down
the stairs and find yourself a rubber chicken. Most summoning monster
spellcasters can be genocided, and Rodney should be on the business end of
a death ray as soon as he appears. Of course this is no guarantee he won't
show up, but it's the first line of defence.

Secondly, as Martin observes, a scroll of scare monster offers the
Elbereth effect. I don't have a problem with this because reblessing the
scroll uses a consumable resource; bSoSM should be part of everyone's
emergency kit. So on very bad things like Demogorgon, the Elbereth effect
is available.

Demogorgon is a perfectly respectable thing to burn the emergency wish on.
Last time I saw him he lasted as long as it took to wish for the rubber
chicken, wield it, and tap him gently on the bonce.

A 100% reliable method of curing sickness is a very valuable thing to
have. Failing that, the combination of a blessed unicorn horn, being Very
Fast, not messing about doing anything else while Sick, and the humble
AoLS as an emergency backup results in a very slow rate of AoLS
consumption. I don't enter Demogorgon territory without having a definite
plan for treating deathly sickness; bear in mind that a Lawful or Neutral
character can consume holy water to cure sickness 100% reliably, and you
should have a huge oversupply of same.

Whenever I meet Demogorgon the first thing I do is refresh my memory of
exactly how fast deathly sickness can kill me. This allows me, if I have a
100% reliable method of curing, to maximise my use of the available turns
to do other things.

The objective, in a fair fight where you are curing yourself at the cost
of consumables or mana, is to turn it into an unfair fight. Ie, the real
objective is to get him to teleport to the upstairs and then immediately
level teleport out of there and find a rubber chicken - or to teleport to
the downstairs, leave the level, and find a rubber chicken - or if you
have a reasonable supply of cure, to descend from the level above and
occupy the upstairs. If you've got the Amulet and want to level teleport,
ditch the thing, it'll be around when you get back.

One idea that springs to mind is that if you have the Amulet you can buy
yourself a few turns by throwing it away from you, which might be just
long enough to escape the level. Better yet if Rodney has just summoned
Demogorgon and you can arrange for Rodney to get it, perhaps by throwing
it at him - then Demogorgon will pound on Rodney and you have bought more
than a few turns.]

